  "next_id": 28,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -30,
        -12
      ],
      "id": 27,
      "text": "CC/CV charger for one Li-ion cell with an LM317 (1000 mAh with 150 mOhm + 150 mOhm inside, starting at 20 %, time accelerated 120 times: an hour in 30 s).\nCV: R1 and R2 set 4.2 V across the cell (R2 returns to its - terminal, so RS is outside the loop). CC: above about 0.55 A the drop on RS (1.2 ohm) turns Q1 on, which pulls ADJ down.\nWatch the battery's current and voltage in the Signal Analyzer: constant current, then constant voltage while the current falls;\nthe battery shows its state of charge. With protection, charging would stop above 4.25 V per cell."
    }
  ],
